From b3de18494af0b5f856299af5197dc39477d87ee5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:21:38 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] fix(setup): refuse generation under a WCS tilted off the
 machine Z

A milling setup's WCS could be turned onto another face, but every
milling generator cuts along the machine's Z, so the toolpath machined
the part as it lies (the wrong face) and reported OK; only the post's
rotated-offset clause (#315) held it back. Generation now refuses a WCS
whose Z is tilted off the machine's, by name, pointing at the setup's
Part alignment, and a facing pick on a face that is level only in the
tilted WCS says the WCS is why. A WCS turned only about Z still
generates.

Fixes #1510

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
